=\"REL\"><mo>:=</mo></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mo>/</mo></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>∈</mo><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">Q</mi></mrow></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span>.</p>\n<div class=\"enumerate\" data-options=\"label=(\\alph*)\">\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li>Show that <span class=\"math inline\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\" data-tex=\"(q_n)\"><mjx-math class=\" MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c28\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-msub><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D45E TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: -0.15em; margin-left: -0.014em;\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\" size=\"s\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D45B TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-script></mjx-msub><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c29\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span> is a Cauchy\nsequence of rationals and that <span class=\"math inline\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\" data-tex=\"[(q_n)] =\n1\"><mjx-math class=\" MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c5B\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c28\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-msub><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D45E TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: -0.15em; margin-left: -0.014em;\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\" size=\"s\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D45B TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-script></mjx-msub><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c29\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c5D\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c3D\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span> in <span class=\"math inline\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb{R}\"><mjx-math class=\" MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-TeXAtom texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-ds mjx-b\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c211D TEX-A\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-TeXAtom></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">R</mi></mrow></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span>.</li>\n<li>Every <span class=\"math inline\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\" data-tex=\"q_n\"><mjx-math class=\" MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-msub><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D45E TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: -0.15em; margin-left: -0.014em;\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\" size=\"s\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D45B TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-script></mjx-msub></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span> is less than <span class=\"math inline\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\" data-tex=\"1\"><mjx-math class=\" MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span>. What inequality between <span class=\"math inline\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\" data-tex=\"[(q_n)]\"><mjx-math class=\" MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c5B\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c28\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-msub><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D45E TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: -0.15em; margin-left: -0.014em;\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\" size=\"s\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D45B TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-script></mjx-msub><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c29\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c5D\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span> and <span class=\"math inline\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\" data-tex=\"1\"><mjx-math class=\" MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span> does a termwise comparison give, and\nwhy can it not give a strict one?</li>\n</ol>\n</div>","file":"ch6/the-uniqueness-theorem.html"}